	(text_box "For MISO we need to only output a signal if one of the chips on this card is selected, so we need to use tri-state buffer and only enable the output based on CS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 151.13 0)
		(size 34.29 13.97)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "02c66e36-218d-4ae7-a13e-322e4513e14f")
	)
	(text_box "This SN74AHC device runs off 3.3V power but accepts input logic voltages of up to 7 V. This means it can be used to shift down from 5V to 3.3V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.78 148.59 0)
		(size 38.1 12.7)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b9f18ed9-3683-488f-9d53-311677a9594e")
	)
	(text_box "TXB0106 level shifter shifts from 1.2-3.6V to 1.65-5.5V.\nNote that this is a bidirectional level shifter so it's slightly wacky, it's always driving all I/O lines at all times via a 4kOhm resistor, and when something on either side overpowers that resistor and changes the state of the pin, it causes the logic level to change on both sides of the shifter. That should be OK for this application but it is a little extra for what we need.\nOddly, though, I literally couldn't find a single unidirectional level shifter that met the requirements and had a propagation time better than 150ns!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.81 80.01 0)
		(size 82.55 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc6904a6-4bdd-4e8d-ad56-afc4de115c64")
	)
